// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 10-temporal-validity
// facility: rule.temporal.ref-escape (spec/10 §2), D-0290 (CHG-0439): a `Vec` of references holding `&y`, moved into a binding that outlives `y`; conf.vec-of-refs-moved-out-of-block-rejected
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.destroy-while-aliased (static)
//
// `v` holds `y` (it was pushed `&y`), and `r = v` gives `r` what `v` held:
// `y` ends while `r` is still used. The facts of a `Vec` did not follow
// it into `r`, and the compiled program read `y`'s dead slot.

import std;

fn main()
{
    Vec<ref<i32, shared>> r = Vec::new();
    drop(r);
    {
        i32 y = 2;
        Vec<ref<i32, shared>> v = Vec::new();
        Vec::push(&mut v, &y);
        r = v;
    }
    printf("%v\n", *r[0]);
}
